  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Dima's wife, Kristina, returns early from Monaco. She storms into the restaurant and accuses Dima of having an affair with Vika. Max bravely steps in to defend his boss.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Что ты здесь делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Ты должна быть в Монако!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "А я вернулась!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Ты отправил меня туда специально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Кто эта женщина, Дима?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я ничего не знаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Мне Саша все сказала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Она тут работает и все видит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Можно я скажу?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Виктория Сергеевна — моя девушка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас с ней серьезные отношения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пусть ваша жена извинится перед моей девушкой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Пойдем домой, моя родная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Завтра полетим отдыхать, хорошо?",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around My Girlfriend line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Что ты здесь делаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What are you doing here?' Dima is caught by surprise. We use 'are' in English, but Russian skips it.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Ты должна быть в Монако!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You are supposed to be in Monaco!' The word for 'supposed' or 'must' has a feminine ending, because Dima is talking to a woman.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "А я вернулась!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I came back!' Kristina is furious. The verb is in the past tense feminine.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Ты отправил меня туда специально.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You sent me there on purpose.' The verb is in the past tense masculine, matching 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Кто эта женщина, Дима?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who is this woman, Dima?' She demands to know the truth. The word 'is' is not translated.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я ничего не знаю.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I don't know anything.' Dima plays dumb. Notice the double negative in Russian: 'nothing not know'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Мне Саша все сказала.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Sasha told me everything.' Sasha is the waitress who gossips. The object 'me' comes first.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Она тут работает и все видит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She works here and sees everything.' Kristina trusts the waitress completely. Both verbs are in the present tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Можно я скажу?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Can I say something?' Max steps in to save Vika. Literally, 'Is it possible I will say?'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Виктория Сергеевна — моя девушка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Victoria Sergeyevna is my girlfriend.' Max uses Vika's formal name to show respect. The word for 'is' is replaced by a dash in writing.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас с ней серьезные отношения.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a serious relationship.' Literally, 'By us with her are serious relations'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Пусть ваша жена извинится перед моей девушкой!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let your wife apologize to my girlfriend!' Max demands respect. The word for 'let' is used to make a strong suggestion or command.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Пойдем домой, моя родная.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let's go home, my dear.' Dima quickly tries to defuse the situation. The word for 'dear' is a feminine adjective.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Завтра полетим отдыхать, хорошо?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Tomorrow we will fly to rest, okay?' He promises her a vacation. The verb for 'fly' is in the future tense. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
